# Shared by every build whose context is app/ (the proxy and Airflow). Each Dockerfile COPYs
# only what it names, so this list is about noise and secrets rather than about scoping —
# `api/` was excluded here once and it silently starved Airflow's build of the ingest code.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# D104's build stage runs `npm ci` inside the image, so a `node_modules` from the developer's
# machine must not ride along — it would add several hundred megabytes to every build context
# (the proxy's *and* Airflow's, which share this file) and, worse, `COPY web/ ./` would bury the
# tree `npm ci` had just installed with one resolved on a different platform. The exclusion and
# that COPY belong together; neither is safe alone.
**/node_modules

# A host's TLS material is mounted at run time (compose.yaml, proxy) and must never be baked in.
tls/
